<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - March 7.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - March 7.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 03/07/97  02/28/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     29.94     37.18    12.88	15.99	9.9</p>
<p>West	     56.72     63.30    21.89	24.43     30.1</p>
<p>Total Canada   86.67    100.48    17.63	20.44     20.6</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 03/07/97: 232.55 bcf, 02/28/97: 232.55 bcf. </p>
<p>West capacity 03/07/97: 259.11 bcf, 02/28/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
